# CINTEXA CCDI — environment configuration template
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# The web client (public/) gets its Firebase config directly from
# public/assets/js/core/firebase-config.js (Firebase web config is not a
# secret — it identifies the project, not a credential). This file is for
# Cloud Functions runtime configuration and any connector credentials your
# OWN scanner infrastructure needs. Never commit a filled-in copy of this
# file; commit only .env.example.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Firebase / GCP ---
FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=your-project-id

# --- Vulnerability intelligence sources (public APIs; no key required by
#     default, but set these if you have an NVD API key for higher rate
#     limits: https://nvd.nist.gov/developers/request-an-api-key) ---
NVD_API_KEY=

# --- Connector credentials (referenced, never embedded in Firestore) ---
# Store actual secrets in Google Secret Manager and reference them from the
# Connectors page via a secretmanager://... style reference string.
# Example:
# ZAP_API_KEY=
# BURP_ENTERPRISE_API_TOKEN=

# --- Email provider for user invitations (wire up in functions/src/routes/users.js) ---
# SENDGRID_API_KEY=
# EMAIL_FROM=security@yourcompany.com
